      "On the freight we pass on to you",
      "On the transport cost shown in the quotation.",
      "Set price",
      "On à la carte services",
      "Supplier visit, 10 suppliers in 3 days, guided trips to China: the price shown on this page. Product testing: on quotation.",
      "None",
      "Admin or subscription fees",
      "Getting a quotation, opening an account, entrusting us with an order: nothing to pay on top of the commission.",
      "The 2% and 3% rates don’t vary with the value of the order: no tiers, no case-by-case discounts. If you buy directly from your suppliers, only the 3% on the freight applies.",
      "Sourcing for orders placed through SourcingPick remains included in the commission. À la carte services are optional: they are paid for at the price shown, whether or not an order follows.",
      "What affects a quotation",
      "The volume and weight of your goods",
      "The number of suppliers to consolidate",
      "The level of inspection you ask for",
      "Whether you need wooden crates",
      "The port of destination and the season",
      "What every quotation includes",
      "Each service on a separate line",
      "Ocean freight at the current rate, shown separately",
      "Payment terms",
      "How long the quotation is valid: 7 to 30 days",
      "Our commission, on its own line",
      "Payment",
      "A deposit of 40% on order, the balance before the container is loaded.",
      "By bank transfer or card, directly from your client area.",
      "Questions about pricing",
      "Why are shipping prices indicative?",
      "Because freight rates change every week with the market. The prices shown are a guide for comparing transport modes. The actual price is shown separately, on your quotation.",
      "Is the quotation free?",
      "Yes. The quotation is free and without obligation, whatever the volume.",
      "Can I pay in instalments?",
      "A deposit of 40% on order, then the balance before the container is loaded.",
      "Why do you recommend sea freight?",
      "It’s the cheapest of the four modes, at 7.4 to 18.9 RMB per volumetric kilo. Road freight is riskier and rail costs barely less than road: we recommend neither. Air freight is still useful for a small, urgent package.",
      "What is a volumetric kilo?",
      "We compare a package’s actual weight with its volume converted into kilos. The higher of the two is used as the basis for the price. So a light but bulky carton costs more than you might think.",
      "What do you do on a supplier visit?",
      "We go there in person, check that the company and its products match the listing, then negotiate the price in Chinese. You receive a report with photos and video, and our opinion.",
      "Does the “10 suppliers in 3 days” pack include visits?",
      "Yes. In three days, we visit ten suppliers in Guangdong on your behalf, for €1,900, including food, travel and hotel. For each one, you receive photos, video, price, minimum order quantity and lead times. For more than ten suppliers, we draw up a quotation.",
      "What does a guided trip to China include?",
      "A schedule of factory visits and supplier meetings, with us at your side to translate and negotiate, help with your visa and free access to the SourcingPick app. Flights, hotel, meals and travel are at your own expense.",
      "How does product testing work?",
      "You place your order through us. We receive the goods in Guangzhou, open the cartons and test your products against your criteria. You receive photos, videos and a report before shipment. The price depends on the product and the number of items tested: it is given on quotation.",
      "Tell us about your next order.",
      "You’ll receive a detailed quotation within 24 to 72 hours, in French, English or Chinese.",
      "Request a quotation",
      "contact@sourcingpick.com",
      "We’ll handle the rest!",
